{
  "schema": "prova.verification-case/1",
  "title": "Panel graphical VAR, saturated model",
  "description": "The saturated panel graphical VAR (temporal, contemporaneous and between-person networks) of a simulated panel: 400 persons, four waves, three variables (the package's fixture design \"default\"), by maximum likelihood without pruning. The reference is psychonetrics::panelgvar() |> runmodel() on the same data, kept in tests/testthat/fixtures/psychonetrics-panelgvar.rds (psychonetrics is not installed here, so its side is retained, not rerun). The fixture holds the 24 estimates and standard errors as bare vectors in psychonetrics' parameter order; they are named here by position from psychnets' parameter table, the pairing the package's own test uses. psychnets is called with the long panel; the fixture was made from the same panel in wide form.",
